+  "snippet": "tags: z.string().describe('Up to three lowercase topic tags, comma separated'),",
+  "cause": "The summarizeTicket output schema declares tags as a single string with a comma-separated description, so the model's structured output is a string instead of the list of tags the dashboard expects.",
+  "evidence": "src/flows.ts line 8 defines tags as z.string(), and TicketSummarySchema is used as summarizeTicket's outputSchema (line 13) and as the generate output schema (line 20), so the model is constrained to return a comma-joined string; it is the only tags definition in the project. After changing it to z.array(z.string()), npx tsc --noEmit reports no errors. The triage dashboard is not in this repo, so its list handling was not checked directly."
+}
